aristotle-ethics-4.logic.r1: argue/scope: A1: read with the obligation on its consequent alone, O discriminate → O observe_practicable, the argument holds; read with it on the whole conditional, O(O discriminate → observe_practicable), C (S3) does not follow: it needs the ought on the consequent alone (narrow scope), not only on the conditional (wide), and which the sentence means decides the argument
aristotle-ethics-4.logic.r1: argue/scope: P3 (S3): read with the obligation on its consequent alone, diff_class_harder ∧ O discriminate → O ¬give_up, the argument holds; read with it on the whole conditional, O(diff_class_harder ∧ O discriminate → ¬give_up), C (S3) does not follow: it needs the ought on the consequent alone (narrow scope), not only on the conditional (wide), and which the sentence means decides the argument
